PathwayData.put("data/grammar_vocabulary/units/L01U6.json",{"strand":"grammar_vocabulary","level":1,"cefr":"A1a","unit":6,"theme":"Fun and Games","essential_question":"Why is it good to play together?","lessons":[{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS1","title":"I Can Swim! can / can't for Ability","objectives":["Students will be able to say what people can and can't do with can + verb.","Students will be able to ask and answer Can you…? questions.","I can say \"I can swim\" and \"I can't ride a horse\".","I can ask \"Can you jump high?\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من قول ما يستطيع الناس وما لا يستطيعون فعله باستخدام can + الفعل.","سيتمكن الطلاب من طرح سؤال Can you…? والإجابة عنه.","أستطيع أن أقول I can swim وI can't ride a horse.","أستطيع أن أسأل Can you jump high?"],"vocabulary":[{"word":"run","pos":"verb","ipa":"/rʌn/","definition":"to move very fast on your feet","arabic":"يركض","example":"I run around the park with my dad.","image_id":"GV-L01-U6-LS1-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U6-LS1-W01"},{"word":"jump","pos":"verb","ipa":"/dʒʌmp/","definition":"to push your body up into the air","arabic":"يقفز","example":"Kangaroos jump on their strong legs.","image_id":"GV-L01-U6-LS1-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U6-LS1-W02"},{"word":"swim","pos":"verb","ipa":"/swɪm/","definition":"to move through water with your arms and legs","arabic":"يسبح","example":"Ducks swim on the lake.","image_id":"GV-L01-U6-LS1-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U6-LS1-W03"},{"word":"climb","pos":"verb","ipa":"/klaɪm/","definition":"to go up something using your hands and feet","arabic":"يتسلّق","example":"The boys climb the rope in the gym.","image_id":"GV-L01-U6-LS1-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U6-LS1-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"We use can to say that someone is able to do something: I can swim. We use can't (cannot) when someone is not able: I can't fly.\ncan is the same for everyone: I can, he can, they can. After can, use the base verb: She can run (NOT She can runs / She can to run).\nFor questions, put can first: Can you swim? – Yes, I can. / No, I can't.","examples":["I can climb a tree.","My little brother can't read yet.","Penguins can't fly, but they can swim.","Can you catch a ball? – Yes, I can.","We can play football after school.","My grandma can make delicious bread.","Fish can't walk.","Can your cousin ride a horse? – No, he can't."],"common_errors":["✗ He can swims. → ✓ He can swim. (After can, use the base verb (no -s).)","✗ I can to ride a bike. → ✓ I can ride a bike. (No to after can.)","✗ You can swim? → ✓ Can you swim? (In questions, can comes first.)"],"arabic":"نستخدم can للتعبير عن القدرة (يستطيع)، وcan't للتعبير عن عدم القدرة (لا يستطيع).\ncan لا تتغير مع الضمائر: I can / he can، وبعدها الفعل في صورته الأصلية: He can swim (وليس swims).\nلا نضع to بعد can: I can ride وليس I can to ride.\nفي السؤال نبدأ بـ can: Can you swim?"},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “I Can Swim! can / can't for Ability”. Let’s learn can / can't for ability together.","on_screen":"GV-L01-U6-LS1 | I Can Swim! can / can't for Ability","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Listen to the start of “Sports Day”: Today is Sports Day! I'm Omar, and I can run very fast. Look at the green words.","on_screen":"Today is Sports Day! I'm Omar, and I can run very fast.","visual":"Image GV-L01-U6-LS1-IMG01 animates gently; target words glow Leaf Green as they are spoken."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"We use can to say that someone is able to do something: I can swim. We use can't (cannot) when someone is not able: I can't fly. can is the same for everyone: I can, he can, they can. After can, use the base verb: She can run (NOT She can runs / She can to run).","on_screen":"can / can't for ability","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. I can climb a tree. My little brother can't read yet. Penguins can't fly, but they can swim.","on_screen":"I can climb a tree. / My little brother can't read yet. / Penguins can't fly, but they can swim.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “He can swims.” That’s not right. We say: “He can swim.” After can, use the base verb (no -s).","on_screen":"✗ He can swims.   ✓ He can swim.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"Penguins can't fly.\" Are penguins able to fly? … Think! … No, they aren't. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"I can swim\" and \"I can't ride a horse\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"I can swim\" and \"I can't ride a horse\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: can / can't for ability.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نستخدم can للتعبير عن القدرة (يستطيع)، وcan't للتعبير عن عدم القدرة (لا يستطيع).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: He can swims. — الصحيح: He can swim.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول I can swim وI can't ride a horse."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Sports Day","body":"Today is Sports Day! I'm Omar, and I can run very fast.\nMy friend Yusuf can jump high, but he can't swim.\nAdam can kick the ball into the goal. Goal!\nMr. Khalid can blow the whistle very loudly!\nCan you ride a bike? I can ride a bike, but I can't ride a horse.\nOur team can win the race today!","word_count":62,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U6-LS1-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"Birds ___ fly.","options":["can't","cans","can to","can"],"answer":"can","explanation":"can = able to; it is the same for all subjects.","explanation_ar":"can تعني يستطيع ولا تتغير."},{"q":"A fish ___ climb trees.","options":["can","not can","can't","cans"],"answer":"can't","explanation":"can't = not able to.","explanation_ar":"can't تعني لا يستطيع."},{"q":"My sister can ___ very well.","options":["draw","draws","to draw","drawing"],"answer":"draw","explanation":"After can/can't, use the base verb (no -s, no to).","explanation_ar":"بعد can نستخدم الفعل الأصلي."},{"q":"___ you swim? – Yes, I can.","options":["Is","Can","Are","Do"],"answer":"Can","explanation":"Questions: Can + subject + verb?","explanation_ar":"السؤال: Can ثم الفاعل ثم الفعل."},{"q":"Can your dad cook? – No, he ___.","options":["can","isn't","doesn't","can't"],"answer":"can't","explanation":"can't = not able to.","explanation_ar":"can't تعني لا يستطيع."},{"q":"Monkeys can ___ trees easily.","options":["climb","to climb","climbing","climbs"],"answer":"climb","explanation":"After can/can't, use the base verb (no -s, no to).","explanation_ar":"بعد can نستخدم الفعل الأصلي."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS1-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Make sentences with can or can't.","items":[{"q":"a horse / run fast (✔)  (can)","options":[],"answer":"A horse can run fast.","explanation":"can = able to; it is the same for all subjects.","explanation_ar":"can تعني يستطيع ولا تتغير."},{"q":"a baby / ride a bike (✘)  (can't)","options":[],"answer":"A baby can't ride a bike.","explanation":"can't = not able to.","explanation_ar":"can't تعني لا يستطيع."},{"q":"dolphins / swim (✔)  (can)","options":[],"answer":"Dolphins can swim.","explanation":"can = able to; it is the same for all subjects.","explanation_ar":"can تعني يستطيع ولا تتغير."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS1-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Make questions with Can.","items":[{"q":"you / touch your toes  (question)","options":[],"answer":"Can you touch your toes?","explanation":"Questions: Can + subject + verb?","explanation_ar":"السؤال: Can ثم الفاعل ثم الفعل."},{"q":"your brother / play chess  (question)","options":[],"answer":"Can your brother play chess?","explanation":"Questions: Can + subject + verb?","explanation_ar":"السؤال: Can ثم الفاعل ثم الفعل."},{"q":"Sara / speak English  (question)","options":[],"answer":"Can Sara speak English?","explanation":"Questions: Can + subject + verb?","explanation_ar":"السؤال: Can ثم الفاعل ثم الفعل."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS1-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Write about you.","items":[{"q":"I can ___.","options":[],"answer":"I can swim.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses can / can't for ability correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I can't ___.","options":[],"answer":"I can't ride a horse.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses can / can't for ability correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"My friend can ___ very well.","options":[],"answer":"My friend can play football very well.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses can / can't for ability correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"My mom can ___.","options":[],"answer":"My mom can make kabsa.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses can / can't for ability correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I can ___, but I can't ___.","options":[],"answer":"I can run fast, but I can't jump high.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses can / can't for ability correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS1-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Ability survey.","items":[{"q":"Ask 3 classmates \"Can you…?\" questions. Write their answers.","options":[],"answer":"Saad can swim. Ali can't ride a horse. Fahad can climb a rope.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses can / can't for ability correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences about an animal: what it can and can't do.","options":[],"answer":"A camel can walk in the desert. It can't fly.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses can / can't for ability correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one thing you want to learn. Use \"I can't … yet.\"","options":[],"answer":"I can't ride a horse yet.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses can / can't for ability correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Four Corners Grammar","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["The teacher says a sentence frame with a cue word and four possible answers (A–D).","Students walk to the corner with the correct answer.","One student in each corner explains the choice in one sentence.","Correct corner scores a point; continue with the next cue."],"data":[{"label":"I"},{"label":"my dad"},{"label":"a fish"},{"label":"we"},{"label":"my little sister"},{"label":"birds"},{"label":"you"},{"label":"a camel"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"Kangaroos ___ jump very high.","options":["can to","can","cans","can't"],"answer":"can","explanation":"can = able to; it is the same for all subjects.","explanation_ar":"can تعني يستطيع ولا تتغير."},{"q":"My baby sister ___ walk yet.","options":["cans","can't","can","not can"],"answer":"can't","explanation":"can't = not able to.","explanation_ar":"can't تعني لا يستطيع."},{"q":"He can ___ the ball.","options":["throwing","throws","to throw","throw"],"answer":"throw","explanation":"After can/can't, use the base verb (no -s, no to).","explanation_ar":"بعد can نستخدم الفعل الأصلي."},{"q":"___ they play basketball?","options":["Do","Is","Can","Are"],"answer":"Can","explanation":"Questions: Can + subject + verb?","explanation_ar":"السؤال: Can ثم الفاعل ثم الفعل."},{"q":"Can you speak Arabic? – Yes, I ___.","options":["can't","do","can","am"],"answer":"can","explanation":"can = able to; it is the same for all subjects.","explanation_ar":"can تعني يستطيع ولا تتغير."},{"q":"","options":["My uncle can to fix cars.","My uncle cans fix cars.","My uncle can fixes cars.","My uncle can fix cars."],"answer":"My uncle can fix cars.","explanation":"After can/can't, use the base verb (no -s, no to).","explanation_ar":"بعد can نستخدم الفعل الأصلي."},{"q":"","options":["Can Turki swim?","Turki can swim?","Can Turki swims?","Turki swim can?"],"answer":"Can Turki swim?","explanation":"Questions: Can + subject + verb?","explanation_ar":"السؤال: Can ثم الفاعل ثم الفعل."},{"q":"A snake ___ run. It has no legs.","options":["cans","can","can't","can to"],"answer":"can't","explanation":"can't = not able to.","explanation_ar":"can't تعني لا يستطيع."},{"q":"Can Lina draw horses? – No, she ___.","options":["can't","doesn't","can","isn't"],"answer":"can't","explanation":"can't = not able to.","explanation_ar":"can't تعني لا يستطيع."},{"q":"","options":["We can climbing the hill.","We can climb the hill.","We cans climb the hill.","We can to climb the hill."],"answer":"We can climb the hill.","explanation":"After can/can't, use the base verb (no -s, no to).","explanation_ar":"بعد can نستخدم الفعل الأصلي."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS1-IMG01","prompt":"Sports Day on the school field: Omar running a race, Yusuf doing a high jump, Adam kicking a ball into a goal, and Mr. Khalid blowing a whistle. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Sports Day on the school field: Omar running a race, Yusuf doing a high jump, Adam kicking a ball into a goal, and Mr. Khalid blowing a whistle"},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS1-IMG02","prompt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about can / can't for ability, with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right; leave large empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about can / can't for ability, with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right"},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS1-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows run (to move very fast on your feet); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing run: to move very fast on your feet"},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS1-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows jump (to push your body up into the air); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing jump: to push your body up into the air"},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS1-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows swim (to move through water with your arms and legs); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing swim: to move through water with your arms and legs"},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS1-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows climb (to go up something using your hands and feet); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing climb: to go up something using your hands and feet"},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS1-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Four Corners Grammar”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Four Corners Grammar"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U6-LS1-W01","script":"run. run. I run around the park with my dad.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U6-LS1-W02","script":"jump. jump. Kangaroos jump on their strong legs.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U6-LS1-W03","script":"swim. swim. Ducks swim on the lake.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U6-LS1-W04","script":"climb. climb. The boys climb the rope in the gym.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U6-LS1-T1","script":"Today is Sports Day! I'm Omar, and I can run very fast. My friend Yusuf can jump high, but he can't swim. Adam can kick the ball into the goal. Goal! Mr. Khalid can blow the whistle very loudly! Can you ride a bike? I can ride a bike, but I can't ride a horse. Our team can win the race today!","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U6-LS1-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “I Can Swim! can / can't for Ability”. Let’s learn can / can't for ability together. Listen to the start of “Sports Day”: Today is Sports Day! I'm Omar, and I can run very fast. Look at the green words. We use can to say that someone is able to do something: I can swim. We use can't (cannot) when someone is not able: I can't fly. can is the same for everyone: I can, he can, they can. After can, use the base verb: She can run (NOT She can runs / She can to run). Here are some examples. I can climb a tree. My little brother can't read yet. Penguins can't fly, but they can swim. Be careful! Some learners say: “He can swims.” That’s not right. We say: “He can swim.” After can, use the base verb (no -s). Quick check: \"Penguins can't fly.\" Are penguins able to fly? … Think! … No, they aren't. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"I can swim\" and \"I can't ride a horse\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS2","title":"Stop! Go! Wait! Imperatives","objectives":["Students will be able to give instructions with the base verb (Run! Sit down!).","Students will be able to give negative rules with Don't + verb.","I can give instructions like \"Pass the ball!\"","I can give rules like \"Don't push!\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من إعطاء التعليمات بالفعل الأصلي (Run! Sit down!).","سيتمكن الطلاب من إعطاء قواعد النهي باستخدام Don't + الفعل.","أستطيع أن أعطي تعليمات مثل Pass the ball!","أستطيع أن أعطي قواعد مثل Don't push!"],"vocabulary":[{"word":"throw","pos":"verb","ipa":"/θroʊ/","definition":"to send something through the air with your hand","arabic":"يرمي","example":"Throw the ball to Majed!","image_id":"GV-L01-U6-LS2-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U6-LS2-W01"},{"word":"catch","pos":"verb","ipa":"/kætʃ/","definition":"to take something that is moving in the air","arabic":"يمسك / يلتقط","example":"The goalkeeper can catch the ball.","image_id":"GV-L01-U6-LS2-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U6-LS2-W02"},{"word":"kick","pos":"verb","ipa":"/kɪk/","definition":"to hit something with your foot","arabic":"يركل","example":"He kicks the ball very hard.","image_id":"GV-L01-U6-LS2-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U6-LS2-W03"},{"word":"ride","pos":"verb","ipa":"/raɪd/","definition":"to sit on and control a bike or a horse","arabic":"يركب","example":"My cousin rides his bike to the shop.","image_id":"GV-L01-U6-LS2-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U6-LS2-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"We use imperatives to tell people what to do. Start with the base verb – there is no subject: Kick the ball! Sit down.\nTo tell people what not to do, use Don't + base verb: Don't run in the hall!\nAdd please to be polite: Please sit down. / Sit down, please.","examples":["Throw the ball to me!","Don't kick the chairs.","Stand in a line, please.","Drink water after the race.","Don't forget your hat.","Please wait here.","Listen to the whistle!","Don't play near the road."],"common_errors":["✗ Not run! → ✓ Don't run! (Negative imperative = Don't + verb.)","✗ You sit down. → ✓ Sit down. (Imperatives have no subject.)","✗ Please to listen. → ✓ Please listen. (No to after please.)"],"arabic":"نستخدم صيغة الأمر بالفعل الأصلي بدون فاعل: Sit down! (اجلس).\nللنهي نستخدم Don't + الفعل: Don't run! (لا تركض) وليس Not run.\nلنكون مهذبين نضيف please: Please sit down."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Stop! Go! Wait! Imperatives”. Let’s learn imperatives (do / don't) for rules and instructions together.","on_screen":"GV-L01-U6-LS2 | Stop! Go! Wait! Imperatives","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Remember these patterns: Pass the ball! • Wait for your turn. • Please listen. Don't push. • Don't shout. • Please don't touch. (no question form – we ask with \"Can you…?\": Can you pass the ball, please?)","on_screen":"Pass the ball! • Wait for your turn. • Please listen. | Don't push. • Don't shout. • Please don't touch. | (no question form – we ask with \"Can you…?\": Can you pass the ball, please?)","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"We use imperatives to tell people what to do. Start with the base verb – there is no subject: Kick the ball! Sit down. To tell people what not to do, use Don't + base verb: Don't run in the hall!","on_screen":"imperatives (do / don't) for rules and instructions","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Throw the ball to me! Don't kick the chairs. Stand in a line, please.","on_screen":"Throw the ball to me! / Don't kick the chairs. / Stand in a line, please.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “Not run!.” That’s not right. We say: “Don't run!.” Negative imperative = Don't + verb.","on_screen":"✗ Not run!   ✓ Don't run!","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: In \"Pass the ball!\", who passes the ball? … Think! … You – the listener. Great job! Now you can say: I can give instructions like \"Pass the ball!\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can give instructions like \"Pass the ball!\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: imperatives (do / don't) for rules and instructions.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نستخدم صيغة الأمر بالفعل الأصلي بدون فاعل: Sit down! (اجلس).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: Not run! — الصحيح: Don't run!","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أعطي تعليمات مثل Pass the ball!"]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"___ the ball to Rakan!","options":["You pass","Passes","To pass","Pass"],"answer":"Pass","explanation":"Imperative = base verb at the start (no subject).","explanation_ar":"الأمر يبدأ بالفعل الأصلي بدون فاعل."},{"q":"___ push your friends.","options":["Don't","No","Doesn't","Not"],"answer":"Don't","explanation":"Negative imperative = Don't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"النهي = Don't + الفعل."},{"q":"Please ___ quietly.","options":["to walk","walks","walk","walking"],"answer":"walk","explanation":"Add please to be polite (no to).","explanation_ar":"أضف please للتأدب."},{"q":"___ your helmet on your bike.","options":["You wear","Wears","Wear","Wearing"],"answer":"Wear","explanation":"Imperative = base verb at the start (no subject).","explanation_ar":"الأمر يبدأ بالفعل الأصلي بدون فاعل."},{"q":"___ play with fire!","options":["Not","Don't","No","Isn't"],"answer":"Don't","explanation":"Negative imperative = Don't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"النهي = Don't + الفعل."},{"q":"___ the whistle and stop.","options":["Listening for","To listen for","Listens for","Listen for"],"answer":"Listen for","explanation":"Imperative = base verb at the start (no subject).","explanation_ar":"الأمر يبدأ بالفعل الأصلي بدون فاعل."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS2-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Make negative rules.","items":[{"q":"Run in the classroom.  (negative)","options":[],"answer":"Don't run in the classroom.","explanation":"Negative imperative = Don't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"النهي = Don't + الفعل."},{"q":"Eat in the library.  (negative)","options":[],"answer":"Don't eat in the library.","explanation":"Negative imperative = Don't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"النهي = Don't + الفعل."},{"q":"Throw stones.  (negative)","options":[],"answer":"Don't throw stones.","explanation":"Negative imperative = Don't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"النهي = Don't + الفعل."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS2-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Make the instructions polite.","items":[{"q":"Close the door.  (polite)","options":[],"answer":"Please close the door.","explanation":"Add please to be polite (no to).","explanation_ar":"أضف please للتأدب."},{"q":"Wait for your turn.  (polite)","options":[],"answer":"Wait for your turn, please.","explanation":"Add please to be polite (no to).","explanation_ar":"أضف please للتأدب."},{"q":"Help me.  (polite)","options":[],"answer":"Please help me.","explanation":"Add please to be polite (no to).","explanation_ar":"أضف please للتأدب."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS2-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Write rules for these places.","items":[{"q":"In the swimming pool: ___.","options":[],"answer":"Don't run near the pool.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses imperatives (do / don't) for rules and instructions correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"In the library: ___.","options":[],"answer":"Please be quiet.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses imperatives (do / don't) for rules and instructions correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"On the football field: ___.","options":[],"answer":"Listen to the coach.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses imperatives (do / don't) for rules and instructions correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"At the park: ___.","options":[],"answer":"Put your trash in the bin.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses imperatives (do / don't) for rules and instructions correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"In the classroom: ___.","options":[],"answer":"Raise your hand to speak.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses imperatives (do / don't) for rules and instructions correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS2-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Make a game rule card.","items":[{"q":"Choose a game you like. Write 3 rules (2 do, 1 don't).","options":[],"answer":"Throw the ball. Catch it with two hands. Don't drop it.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses imperatives (do / don't) for rules and instructions correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 safety rules for riding a bike.","options":[],"answer":"Wear a helmet. Don't ride on busy roads.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses imperatives (do / don't) for rules and instructions correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Read your rules to your team. Write one new rule from a teammate.","options":[],"answer":"Wait for the whistle.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses imperatives (do / don't) for rules and instructions correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Grammar Snakes & Ladders","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["Roll and move. If you land on a cue square, make a sentence with the cue and imperatives (do / don't) for rules and instructions.","Correct at the bottom of a ladder: climb. Incorrect at the head of a snake: slide down.","Teammates are the judges and must explain any correction.","First player to reach square 30 wins."],"data":[{"cue":"Run fast / +"},{"cue":"Push your friends / –"},{"cue":"Listen to the coach / +"},{"cue":"Shout in the library / –"},{"cue":"Catch the ball / +"},{"cue":"Kick the chair / –"},{"cue":"Wait for your turn / +"},{"cue":"Throw stones / –"},{"cue":"Drink water / +"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"___ your hands before lunch.","options":["Washes","Wash","You washes","Washing"],"answer":"Wash","explanation":"Imperative = base verb at the start (no subject).","explanation_ar":"الأمر يبدأ بالفعل الأصلي بدون فاعل."},{"q":"___ talk during the test.","options":["Doesn't","Not","Don't","No"],"answer":"Don't","explanation":"Negative imperative = Don't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"النهي = Don't + الفعل."},{"q":"","options":["Please sit down.","Please sitting down.","Please sits down.","Please to sit down."],"answer":"Please sit down.","explanation":"Add please to be polite (no to).","explanation_ar":"أضف please للتأدب."},{"q":"___ the rope with both hands.","options":["Holds","To hold","Holding","Hold"],"answer":"Hold","explanation":"Imperative = base verb at the start (no subject).","explanation_ar":"الأمر يبدأ بالفعل الأصلي بدون فاعل."},{"q":"","options":["Not cross the street here.","Don't cross the street here.","Don't crosses the street here.","No cross the street here."],"answer":"Don't cross the street here.","explanation":"Negative imperative = Don't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"النهي = Don't + الفعل."},{"q":"Which one is an instruction?","options":["Kick the ball.","The ball is big.","He can kick the ball.","He kicks the ball."],"answer":"Kick the ball.","explanation":"Imperative = base verb at the start (no subject).","explanation_ar":"الأمر يبدأ بالفعل الأصلي بدون فاعل."},{"q":"","options":["You waits for the green light.","Waiting for the green light.","Wait for the green light.","Waits for the green light."],"answer":"Wait for the green light.","explanation":"Imperative = base verb at the start (no subject).","explanation_ar":"الأمر يبدأ بالفعل الأصلي بدون فاعل."},{"q":"___ forget your water bottle.","options":["Not","Don't","Doesn't","No"],"answer":"Don't","explanation":"Negative imperative = Don't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"النهي = Don't + الفعل."},{"q":"","options":["Close the window, please.","Please to close the window.","Close the window, please to.","Closes the window, please."],"answer":"Close the window, please.","explanation":"Add please to be polite (no to).","explanation_ar":"أضف please للتأدب."},{"q":"Which sign is a rule for the pool?","options":["No diving you.","Not dive here.","Dives here.","Don't dive here."],"answer":"Don't dive here.","explanation":"Negative imperative = Don't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"النهي = Don't + الفعل."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS2-IMG01","prompt":"A coach on a football pitch holding a clipboard and whistle, giving instructions to a team of boys in green shirts; a sign with game rules on the fence. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A coach on a football pitch holding a clipboard and whistle, giving instructions to a team of boys in green shirts; a sign with game rules on the fence"},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS2-IMG02","prompt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of imperatives (do / don't) for rules and instructions: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “Fun and Games”; empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of imperatives (do / don't) for rules and instructions: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “Fun and Games”"},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS2-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows throw (to send something through the air with your hand); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing throw: to send something through the air with your hand"},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS2-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows catch (to take something that is moving in the air); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing catch: to take something that is moving in the air"},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS2-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows kick (to hit something with your foot); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing kick: to hit something with your foot"},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS2-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows ride (to sit on and control a bike or a horse); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing ride: to sit on and control a bike or a horse"},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS2-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Grammar Snakes & Ladders”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Grammar Snakes & Ladders"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U6-LS2-W01","script":"throw. throw. Throw the ball to Majed!","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U6-LS2-W02","script":"catch. catch. The goalkeeper can catch the ball.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U6-LS2-W03","script":"kick. kick. He kicks the ball very hard.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U6-LS2-W04","script":"ride. ride. My cousin rides his bike to the shop.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U6-LS2-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Stop! Go! Wait! Imperatives”. Let’s learn imperatives (do / don't) for rules and instructions together. Remember these patterns: Pass the ball! • Wait for your turn. • Please listen. Don't push. • Don't shout. • Please don't touch. (no question form – we ask with \"Can you…?\": Can you pass the ball, please?) We use imperatives to tell people what to do. Start with the base verb – there is no subject: Kick the ball! Sit down. To tell people what not to do, use Don't + base verb: Don't run in the hall! Here are some examples. Throw the ball to me! Don't kick the chairs. Stand in a line, please. Be careful! Some learners say: “Not run!.” That’s not right. We say: “Don't run!.” Negative imperative = Don't + verb. Quick check: In \"Pass the ball!\", who passes the ball? … Think! … You – the listener. Great job! Now you can say: I can give instructions like \"Pass the ball!\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS3","title":"Action Words: Run, Race, and Climb","objectives":["Students will be able to use action verbs for sports and games.","Students will be able to show shades of meaning between verbs like walk, run and race.","I can use action words for sports.","I can choose between walk, run and race."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام أفعال الحركة للرياضة والألعاب.","سيتمكن الطلاب من إظهار درجات المعنى بين أفعال مثل walk وrun وrace.","أستطيع أن أستخدم أفعال الحركة للرياضة.","أستطيع أن أختار بين walk وrun وrace."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"team","pos":"noun","ipa":"/tim/","definition":"a group of people who play together","arabic":"فريق","example":"Our team wears green shirts.","image_id":"GV-L01-U6-LS3-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U6-LS3-W01"},{"word":"goal","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɡoʊl/","definition":"the net where you score in football; a point","arabic":"مرمى / هدف","example":"Saad scores a goal!","image_id":"GV-L01-U6-LS3-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U6-LS3-W02"},{"word":"whistle","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈwɪsəl/","definition":"a small thing you blow to make a loud sound","arabic":"صافرة","example":"The coach blows his whistle.","image_id":"GV-L01-U6-LS3-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U6-LS3-W03"},{"word":"race","pos":"noun","ipa":"/reɪs/","definition":"a game to see who is the fastest","arabic":"سباق","example":"The race starts at nine o'clock.","image_id":"GV-L01-U6-LS3-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U6-LS3-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"Action verbs tell us what someone does: run, jump, swim, climb, throw, catch, kick, ride.\nSome verbs are similar but stronger: walk (slow) → run (fast) → race (as fast as you can to win). This is called shades of meaning.\nSome verbs go in pairs: you throw a ball and your friend catches it.\nCollocations/phrases: walk → run → race • say → shout • look → stare | pairs: throw ↔ catch • win ↔ lose • start ↔ finish | kick a ball • ride a bike • climb a rope • swim in a pool • score a goal • blow a whistle","examples":["The goalkeeper catches the ball.","Players kick the ball with their feet.","Children race to the finish line.","My brother rides his bike to school.","Our team has eleven players.","The referee blows the whistle.","Ziyad scores a great goal!","We climb the hill on Friday."],"common_errors":["✗ I play bike. → ✓ I ride a bike. (We ride a bike or a horse.)","✗ He shoots the ball with his hand. → ✓ He throws the ball. (With your hand, you throw.)","✗ She makes swimming. → ✓ She swims. / She goes swimming. (Use the action verb.)"],"arabic":"أفعال الحركة: run (يركض) وjump (يقفز) وswim (يسبح) وclimb (يتسلق).\nبعض الأفعال أقوى من غيرها: walk (يمشي) ثم run (يركض) ثم race (يتسابق).\nنقول ride a bike (نركب الدراجة) وليس play bike."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Action Words: Run, Race, and Climb”. Let’s learn action verbs and sports words; shades of meaning (walk → run → race) together.","on_screen":"GV-L01-U6-LS3 | Action Words: Run, Race, and Climb","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Meet some new words. team: a group of people who play together. goal: the net where you score in football; a point. whistle: a small thing you blow to make a loud sound.","on_screen":"team | goal | whistle","visual":"Each word card flips over to show its picture (vocabulary image briefs) and Arabic meaning."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Action verbs tell us what someone does: run, jump, swim, climb, throw, catch, kick, ride. Some verbs are similar but stronger: walk (slow) → run (fast) → race (as fast as you can to win). This is called shades of meaning.","on_screen":"action verbs and sports words; shades of meaning (walk → run → race)","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. The goalkeeper catches the ball. Players kick the ball with their feet. Children race to the finish line.","on_screen":"The goalkeeper catches the ball. / Players kick the ball with their feet. / Children race to the finish line.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I play bike.” That’s not right. We say: “I ride a bike.” We ride a bike or a horse.","on_screen":"✗ I play bike.   ✓ I ride a bike.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: Which is faster: walk or race? … Think! … *race* Great job! Now you can say: I can use action words for sports.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can use action words for sports.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: action verbs and sports words; shades of meaning (walk → run → race).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","أفعال الحركة: run (يركض) وjump (يقفز) وswim (يسبح) وclimb (يتسلق).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I play bike. — الصحيح: I ride a bike.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أستخدم أفعال الحركة للرياضة."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"We ___ a ball with our feet.","options":["kick","ride","throw","catch"],"answer":"kick","explanation":"Choose the action that matches the body part or thing.","explanation_ar":"اختر الفعل المناسب."},{"q":"Fish ___ in the sea.","options":["ride","kick","swim","climb"],"answer":"swim","explanation":"Choose the action that matches the body part or thing.","explanation_ar":"اختر الفعل المناسب."},{"q":"I ___ my bike in the park.","options":["play","ride","drive","swim"],"answer":"ride","explanation":"Learn the word partners: ride a bike, kick a ball, score a goal.","explanation_ar":"تعلّم الكلمات المترافقة."},{"q":"Saad throws the ball and I ___ it.","options":["kick","catch","swim","throw"],"answer":"catch","explanation":"throw ↔ catch; win ↔ lose; start ↔ finish.","explanation_ar":"أزواج الأضداد."},{"q":"The coach blows the ___.","options":["goal","race","team","whistle"],"answer":"whistle","explanation":"Learn the word partners: ride a bike, kick a ball, score a goal.","explanation_ar":"تعلّم الكلمات المترافقة."},{"q":"In a ___, everyone runs to win.","options":["goal","rope","race","whistle"],"answer":"race","explanation":"walk (slow) → run (fast) → race (fastest, to win).","explanation_ar":"درجات المعنى من الأبطأ إلى الأسرع."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS3-B1","type":"match","instructions":"Guided practice: Match the verb to the picture description.","items":[{"q":"climb","options":["move in the water","run as fast as you can to win","send a ball with your hand","sit on a horse and go","go up a rope or a tree","go up into the air"],"answer":"go up a rope or a tree","explanation":"climb → go up a rope or a tree. Choose the action that matches the body part or thing.","explanation_ar":"اختر الفعل المناسب."},{"q":"jump","options":["move in the water","run as fast as you can to win","send a ball with your hand","sit on a horse and go","go up a rope or a tree","go up into the air"],"answer":"go up into the air","explanation":"jump → go up into the air. Choose the action that matches the body part or thing.","explanation_ar":"اختر الفعل المناسب."},{"q":"throw","options":["move in the water","run as fast as you can to win","send a ball with your hand","sit on a horse and go","go up a rope or a tree","go up into the air"],"answer":"send a ball with your hand","explanation":"throw → send a ball with your hand. Choose the action that matches the body part or thing.","explanation_ar":"اختر الفعل المناسب."},{"q":"swim","options":["move in the water","run as fast as you can to win","send a ball with your hand","sit on a horse and go","go up a rope or a tree","go up into the air"],"answer":"move in the water","explanation":"swim → move in the water. Choose the action that matches the body part or thing.","explanation_ar":"اختر الفعل المناسب."},{"q":"ride","options":["move in the water","run as fast as you can to win","send a ball with your hand","sit on a horse and go","go up a rope or a tree","go up into the air"],"answer":"sit on a horse and go","explanation":"ride → sit on a horse and go. Choose the action that matches the body part or thing.","explanation_ar":"اختر الفعل المناسب."},{"q":"race","options":["move in the water","run as fast as you can to win","send a ball with your hand","sit on a horse and go","go up a rope or a tree","go up into the air"],"answer":"run as fast as you can to win","explanation":"race → run as fast as you can to win. Choose the action that matches the body part or thing.","explanation_ar":"اختر الفعل المناسب."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS3-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Write about sports you like.","items":[{"q":"I can ___ well.","options":[],"answer":"I can swim well.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses action verbs and sports words; shades of meaning (walk → run → race) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"In football, players ___ the ball.","options":[],"answer":"In football, players kick the ball.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses action verbs and sports words; shades of meaning (walk → run → race) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"My favorite team is ___.","options":[],"answer":"My favorite team is Al-Hilal.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses action verbs and sports words; shades of meaning (walk → run → race) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"At the park, I ___ and ___.","options":[],"answer":"At the park, I run and climb.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses action verbs and sports words; shades of meaning (walk → run → race) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I want to learn to ___.","options":[],"answer":"I want to learn to ride a horse.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses action verbs and sports words; shades of meaning (walk → run → race) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS3-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Action charades.","items":[{"q":"Act out 3 action verbs. Your team guesses. Write the verbs.","options":[],"answer":"swim, climb, throw","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses action verbs and sports words; shades of meaning (walk → run → race) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 3 sentences about a sport using action words.","options":[],"answer":"In basketball, we throw the ball. We jump high. We run fast.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses action verbs and sports words; shades of meaning (walk → run → race) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence with walk, run and race.","options":[],"answer":"I walk to school, I run in the park, and I race my brother.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses action verbs and sports words; shades of meaning (walk → run → race) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Word Dominoes","mechanic":"matching","rules":["Deal the dominoes equally in teams of four.","Player 1 places a domino; the next player adds a domino whose word matches the open definition.","If you cannot play, pass.","The first player with no dominoes left wins."],"data":[{"word":"run","match":"to move very fast on your feet","arabic":"يركض"},{"word":"jump","match":"to push your body up into the air","arabic":"يقفز"},{"word":"swim","match":"to move through water with your arms and legs","arabic":"يسبح"},{"word":"climb","match":"to go up something using your hands and feet","arabic":"يتسلّق"},{"word":"throw","match":"to send something through the air with your hand","arabic":"يرمي"},{"word":"catch","match":"to take something that is moving in the air","arabic":"يمسك / يلتقط"},{"word":"kick","match":"to hit something with your foot","arabic":"يركل"},{"word":"ride","match":"to sit on and control a bike or a horse","arabic":"يركب"},{"word":"team","match":"a group of people who play together","arabic":"فريق"},{"word":"goal","match":"the net where you score in football; a point","arabic":"مرمى / هدف"},{"word":"whistle","match":"a small thing you blow to make a loud sound","arabic":"صافرة"},{"word":"race","match":"a game to see who is the fastest","arabic":"سباق"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"A goalkeeper ___ the ball with his hands.","options":["swims","rides","kicks","catches"],"answer":"catches","explanation":"Choose the action that matches the body part or thing.","explanation_ar":"اختر الفعل المناسب."},{"q":"We ___ up the rope in the gym.","options":["swim","climb","ride","kick"],"answer":"climb","explanation":"Choose the action that matches the body part or thing.","explanation_ar":"اختر الفعل المناسب."},{"q":"She ___ a horse on the farm.","options":["rides","plays","drives","swims"],"answer":"rides","explanation":"Learn the word partners: ride a bike, kick a ball, score a goal.","explanation_ar":"تعلّم الكلمات المترافقة."},{"q":"throw ↔ ___","options":["jump","kick","catch","run"],"answer":"catch","explanation":"throw ↔ catch; win ↔ lose; start ↔ finish.","explanation_ar":"أزواج الأضداد."},{"q":"Which is the fastest?","options":["walk","race","stand","run"],"answer":"race","explanation":"walk (slow) → run (fast) → race (fastest, to win).","explanation_ar":"درجات المعنى من الأبطأ إلى الأسرع."},{"q":"Our ___ wins the cup!","options":["goal","whistle","team","rope"],"answer":"team","explanation":"Learn the word partners: ride a bike, kick a ball, score a goal.","explanation_ar":"تعلّم الكلمات المترافقة."},{"q":"Ali scores a ___. The fans cheer.","options":["team","race","whistle","goal"],"answer":"goal","explanation":"Learn the word partners: ride a bike, kick a ball, score a goal.","explanation_ar":"تعلّم الكلمات المترافقة."},{"q":"win ↔ ___","options":["lose","start","throw","play"],"answer":"lose","explanation":"throw ↔ catch; win ↔ lose; start ↔ finish.","explanation_ar":"أزواج الأضداد."},{"q":"Birds can ___ from tree to tree.","options":["fly","kick","ride","swim"],"answer":"fly","explanation":"Choose the action that matches the body part or thing.","explanation_ar":"اختر الفعل المناسب."},{"q":"","options":["I swim my bike every day.","I play my bike every day.","I ride my bike every day.","I drive my bike every day."],"answer":"I ride my bike every day.","explanation":"Learn the word partners: ride a bike, kick a ball, score a goal.","explanation_ar":"تعلّم الكلمات المترافقة."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS3-IMG01","prompt":"A playground with children doing different actions: climbing a frame, throwing and catching a ball, jumping rope and racing on a track. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A playground with children doing different actions: climbing a frame, throwing and catching a ball, jumping rope and racing on a track"},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS3-IMG02","prompt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 4 small picture icons of the lesson words; empty labels. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 4 small picture icons of the lesson words"},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS3-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows team (a group of people who play together); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing team: a group of people who play together"},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS3-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows goal (the net where you score in football; a point); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing goal: the net where you score in football; a point"},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS3-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows whistle (a small thing you blow to make a loud sound); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing whistle: a small thing you blow to make a loud sound"},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS3-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows race (a game to see who is the fastest); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing race: a game to see who is the fastest"},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS3-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Word Dominoes”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Word Dominoes"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U6-LS3-W01","script":"team. team. Our team wears green shirts.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U6-LS3-W02","script":"goal. goal. Saad scores a goal!","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U6-LS3-W03","script":"whistle. whistle. The coach blows his whistle.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U6-LS3-W04","script":"race. race. The race starts at nine o'clock.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U6-LS3-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Action Words: Run, Race, and Climb”. Let’s learn action verbs and sports words; shades of meaning (walk → run → race) together. Meet some new words. team: a group of people who play together. goal: the net where you score in football; a point. whistle: a small thing you blow to make a loud sound. Action verbs tell us what someone does: run, jump, swim, climb, throw, catch, kick, ride. Some verbs are similar but stronger: walk (slow) → run (fast) → race (as fast as you can to win). This is called shades of meaning. Here are some examples. The goalkeeper catches the ball. Players kick the ball with their feet. Children race to the finish line. Be careful! Some learners say: “I play bike.” That’s not right. We say: “I ride a bike.” We ride a bike or a horse. Quick check: Which is faster: walk or race? … Think! … *race* Great job! Now you can say: I can use action words for sports.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS4","title":"Wow! Great Goal! Exclamation Marks and can't","objectives":["Students will be able to use exclamation marks to show strong feelings and commands.","Students will be able to write the contraction can't with an apostrophe.","I can use an exclamation mark for strong feelings.","I can write can't with an apostrophe."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام علامة التعجب لإظهار المشاعر القوية والأوامر.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة الاختصار can't بالفاصلة العلوية.","أستطيع أن أستخدم علامة التعجب للمشاعر القوية.","أستطيع أن أكتب can't بالفاصلة العلوية."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"run","pos":"verb","ipa":"/rʌn/","definition":"to move very fast on your feet","arabic":"يركض","example":"I run around the park with my dad.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"jump","pos":"verb","ipa":"/dʒʌmp/","definition":"to push your body up into the air","arabic":"يقفز","example":"Kangaroos jump on their strong legs.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"swim","pos":"verb","ipa":"/swɪm/","definition":"to move through water with your arms and legs","arabic":"يسبح","example":"Ducks swim on the lake.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"climb","pos":"verb","ipa":"/klaɪm/","definition":"to go up something using your hands and feet","arabic":"يتسلّق","example":"The boys climb the rope in the gym.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"throw","pos":"verb","ipa":"/θroʊ/","definition":"to send something through the air with your hand","arabic":"يرمي","example":"Throw the ball to Majed!","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"catch","pos":"verb","ipa":"/kætʃ/","definition":"to take something that is moving in the air","arabic":"يمسك / يلتقط","example":"The goalkeeper can catch the ball.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"An exclamation mark (!) shows a strong feeling – surprise, joy, fear – or a loud command: Wow! Great goal! Stop!\nDon't use too many! One exclamation mark is enough: Great! (NOT Great!!!).\nA contraction makes two words shorter. The apostrophe (') shows where letters are missing: can not → can't. In American English we write cannot as one word, or can't.\nStrong feeling → ! : What a great race!\nLoud or urgent command → ! : Look out!\nTelling sentence → . ; question → ?\ncan + not → cannot or can't (apostrophe instead of \"no\")","examples":["Wow! You can jump so high!","Look out! The ball is coming!","I can't find my shoes.","We won the match!","My brother cannot swim yet.","Hurray! It's Sports Day!","Stop! The light is red.","Lina can't come to the park today."],"common_errors":["✗ Great goal!!!! → ✓ Great goal! (One exclamation mark is enough.)","✗ I cant swim. → ✓ I can't swim. (Don't forget the apostrophe.)","✗ I can not ride a horse. → ✓ I cannot / can't ride a horse. (In American English, cannot is one word.)","✗ Wow. → ✓ Wow! (Wow shows strong feeling → !)"],"arabic":"علامة التعجب (!) تُظهر مشاعر قوية مثل الفرح والدهشة، أو أمرًا عاجلًا: Stop!\nلا نكرر علامة التعجب: Great! وليس Great!!!\ncan't اختصار cannot، والفاصلة العلوية (') مكان الحروف المحذوفة. وفي الإنجليزية الأمريكية نكتب cannot كلمة واحدة."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Wow! Great Goal! Exclamation Marks and can't”. Let’s learn exclamation marks (!) and the contraction can't together.","on_screen":"GV-L01-U6-LS4 | Wow! Great Goal! Exclamation Marks and can't","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"An exclamation mark (!) shows a strong feeling – surprise, joy, fear – or a loud command: Wow! Great goal! Stop!","on_screen":"exclamation marks (!) and the contraction can't","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"An exclamation mark (!) shows a strong feeling – surprise, joy, fear – or a loud command: Wow! Great goal! Stop! Don't use too many! One exclamation mark is enough: Great! (NOT Great!!!).","on_screen":"Strong feeling → ! : What a great race! • Loud or urgent command → ! : Look out! • Telling sentence → . ; question → ?","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Wow! You can jump so high! Look out! The ball is coming! I can't find my shoes.","on_screen":"Wow! You can jump so high! / Look out! The ball is coming! / I can't find my shoes.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “Great goal!!!!.” That’s not right. We say: “Great goal!.” One exclamation mark is enough.","on_screen":"✗ Great goal!!!!   ✓ Great goal!","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: Which mark shows strong feeling: . or !? … Think! … *!* Great job! Now you can say: I can use an exclamation mark for strong feelings.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can use an exclamation mark for strong feelings.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: exclamation marks (!) and the contraction can't.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","علامة التعجب (!) تُظهر مشاعر قوية مثل الفرح والدهشة، أو أمرًا عاجلًا: Stop!","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: Great goal!!!! — الصحيح: Great goal!","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أستخدم علامة التعجب للمشاعر القوية."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Our Sports Day (editing passage)","body":"Sports Day was amazing. Saad won the race. Bandar cant jump high, but he can throw far. Our team scored three goals!!! wow! The coach was happy. Can you come next year.","word_count":32,"audio_id":""}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct sentence.","items":[{"q":"","options":["Wow? What a fast car?","Wow!!! What a fast car!!!","Wow. What a fast car.","Wow! What a fast car!"],"answer":"Wow! What a fast car!","explanation":"Strong feeling or urgent command → !","explanation_ar":"المشاعر القوية أو الأمر العاجل ← !"},{"q":"","options":["I can't find my ball.","I ca'nt find my ball.","I can't, find my ball.","I cant find my ball."],"answer":"I can't find my ball.","explanation":"can't = cannot; the apostrophe shows the missing letters.","explanation_ar":"can't اختصار cannot."},{"q":"","options":["Look out! A bee!","look out! a bee!","Look out? A bee?","Look out. A bee."],"answer":"Look out! A bee!","explanation":"Strong feeling or urgent command → !","explanation_ar":"المشاعر القوية أو الأمر العاجل ← !"},{"q":"","options":["My sister cant swim.","My sister cannot swim.","My sister cann't swim.","My sister can not swim."],"answer":"My sister cannot swim.","explanation":"can't = cannot; the apostrophe shows the missing letters.","explanation_ar":"can't اختصار cannot."},{"q":"","options":["hurray! we won!","Hurray! We won!","Hurray. We won.","Hurray!!!! We won!!!!"],"answer":"Hurray! We won!","explanation":"Use only one exclamation mark.","explanation_ar":"علامة تعجب واحدة تكفي."},{"q":"","options":["Can you catch the ball!","can you catch the ball?","Can you catch the ball?","Can you catch the ball."],"answer":"Can you catch the ball?","explanation":"Telling sentence → period; question → question mark.","explanation_ar":"الخبرية بنقطة والسؤال بعلامة استفهام."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS4-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the mistake.","items":[{"q":"We cant play outside today.","options":[],"answer":"We can't play outside today.","explanation":"cant → can't. can't = cannot; the apostrophe shows the missing letters.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: cant → can't. can't اختصار cannot."},{"q":"Stop. The road is busy!","options":[],"answer":"Stop! The road is busy!","explanation":". → !. Strong feeling or urgent command → !","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: . → !. المشاعر القوية أو الأمر العاجل ← !"},{"q":"What a great goal!!!","options":[],"answer":"What a great goal!","explanation":"!!! → !. Use only one exclamation mark.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: !!! → !. علامة تعجب واحدة تكفي."},{"q":"Fahad can not climb the wall.","options":[],"answer":"Fahad cannot climb the wall.","explanation":"can not → cannot. can't = cannot; the apostrophe shows the missing letters.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: can not → cannot. can't اختصار cannot."},{"q":"Wow. You are so fast!","options":[],"answer":"Wow! You are so fast!","explanation":". → !. Strong feeling or urgent command → !","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: . → !. المشاعر القوية أو الأمر العاجل ← !"},{"q":"Can you ride a horse!","options":[],"answer":"Can you ride a horse?","explanation":"! → ?. Telling sentence → period; question → question mark.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: ! → ?. الخبرية بنقطة والسؤال بعلامة استفهام."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS4-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Edit the sports report.","items":[{"q":"Sports Day was amazing. Saad won the race.","options":[],"answer":"Sports Day was amazing! Saad won the race.","explanation":". → !. Strong feeling or urgent command → !","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: . → !. المشاعر القوية أو الأمر العاجل ← !"},{"q":"Bandar cant jump high, but he can throw far.","options":[],"answer":"Bandar can't jump high, but he can throw far.","explanation":"cant → can't. Strong feeling or urgent command → !","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: cant → can't. المشاعر القوية أو الأمر العاجل ← !"},{"q":"Our team scored three goals!!! Wow!","options":[],"answer":"Our team scored three goals! Wow!","explanation":"!!! → !. Strong feeling or urgent command → !","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: !!! → !. المشاعر القوية أو الأمر العاجل ← !"},{"q":"Our team scored three goals! wow!","options":[],"answer":"Our team scored three goals! Wow!","explanation":"wow → Wow. Strong feeling or urgent command → !","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: wow → Wow. المشاعر القوية أو الأمر العاجل ← !"},{"q":"Can you come next year.","options":[],"answer":"Can you come next year?","explanation":". → ?. Strong feeling or urgent command → !","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: . → ?. المشاعر القوية أو الأمر العاجل ← !"}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS4-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write with feeling.","items":[{"q":"Write 2 sentences that show strong feelings about a game.","options":[],"answer":"Great shot! We are the champions!","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses exclamation marks (!) and the contraction can't correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 things you can't do yet. Use can't.","options":[],"answer":"I can't dive. I can't play tennis.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses exclamation marks (!) and the contraction can't correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one urgent command for a safety sign.","options":[],"answer":"Stop! Wear your helmet!","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses exclamation marks (!) and the contraction can't correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Speed Spell","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["The teacher says a word and a short sentence with it.","Students write the word in 10 seconds.","Show boards on \"Show me!\". Correct = 1 point.","After 10 words, partners check each other's boards and correct any mistakes."],"data":[{"word":"run","clue":"to move very fast on your feet"},{"word":"jump","clue":"to push your body up into the air"},{"word":"swim","clue":"to move through water with your arms and legs"},{"word":"climb","clue":"to go up something using your hands and feet"},{"word":"throw","clue":"to send something through the air with your hand"},{"word":"catch","clue":"to take something that is moving in the air"},{"word":"can't","clue":""},{"word":"cannot","clue":""},{"word":"kick","clue":"to hit something with your foot"},{"word":"ride","clue":"to sit on and control a bike or a horse"},{"word":"team","clue":"a group of people who play together"},{"word":"goal","clue":"the net where you score in football; a point"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"","options":["What a great race!","What a great race!!!!","What a great race?","What a great race."],"answer":"What a great race!","explanation":"Strong feeling or urgent command → !","explanation_ar":"المشاعر القوية أو الأمر العاجل ← !"},{"q":"Which mark goes at the end? \"Help__ The cat is in the tree__\"","options":[". / ?","? / .",", / ,","! / !"],"answer":"! / !","explanation":"Strong feeling or urgent command → !","explanation_ar":"المشاعر القوية أو الأمر العاجل ← !"},{"q":"","options":["We ca'nt play today.","We cant play today.","We can't play today.","We can'nt play today."],"answer":"We can't play today.","explanation":"can't = cannot; the apostrophe shows the missing letters.","explanation_ar":"can't اختصار cannot."},{"q":"can + not = ___","options":["can't","cant","cann't","ca'nt"],"answer":"can't","explanation":"can't = cannot; the apostrophe shows the missing letters.","explanation_ar":"can't اختصار cannot."},{"q":"","options":["Watch out. The floor is wet!","watch out! the floor is wet.","Watch out! The floor is wet.","Watch out? The floor is wet?"],"answer":"Watch out! The floor is wet.","explanation":"Strong feeling or urgent command → !","explanation_ar":"المشاعر القوية أو الأمر العاجل ← !"},{"q":"Which sentence needs an exclamation mark?","options":["I am nine years old","My bag is blue","Where is the ball","Hurray, we won"],"answer":"Hurray, we won","explanation":"Strong feeling or urgent command → !","explanation_ar":"المشاعر القوية أو الأمر العاجل ← !"},{"q":"","options":["Wow. Look at that rainbow.","Wow!!! Look at that rainbow!!!","Wow! Look at that rainbow!","Wow? Look at that rainbow?"],"answer":"Wow! Look at that rainbow!","explanation":"Use only one exclamation mark.","explanation_ar":"علامة تعجب واحدة تكفي."},{"q":"","options":["My dad can not come to the match.","My dad cannot come to the match.","My dad cannt come to the match.","My dad can'not come to the match."],"answer":"My dad cannot come to the match.","explanation":"can't = cannot; the apostrophe shows the missing letters.","explanation_ar":"can't اختصار cannot."},{"q":"","options":["Can your team win!","Can your team win?","can your team win?","Can your team win."],"answer":"Can your team win?","explanation":"Telling sentence → period; question → question mark.","explanation_ar":"الخبرية بنقطة والسؤال بعلامة استفهام."},{"q":"Where does the apostrophe go in \"cant\"?","options":["after t","between a and n","between c and a","between n and t"],"answer":"between n and t","explanation":"can't = cannot; the apostrophe shows the missing letters.","explanation_ar":"can't اختصار cannot."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS4-IMG01","prompt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Fun and Games” that shows exclamation marks (!) and the contraction can't in action. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Fun and Games” that shows exclamation marks (!) and the contraction can't in action"},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS4-IMG02","prompt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen"},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS4-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Speed Spell”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Speed Spell"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U6-LS4-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Wow! Great Goal! Exclamation Marks and can't”. Let’s learn exclamation marks (!) and the contraction can't together. An exclamation mark (!) shows a strong feeling – surprise, joy, fear – or a loud command: Wow! Great goal! Stop! An exclamation mark (!) shows a strong feeling – surprise, joy, fear – or a loud command: Wow! Great goal! Stop! Don't use too many! One exclamation mark is enough: Great! (NOT Great!!!). Here are some examples. Wow! You can jump so high! Look out! The ball is coming! I can't find my shoes. Be careful! Some learners say: “Great goal!!!!.” That’s not right. We say: “Great goal!.” One exclamation mark is enough. Quick check: Which mark shows strong feeling: . or !? … Think! … *!* Great job! Now you can say: I can use an exclamation mark for strong feelings.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS5","title":"Our Sports Day Poster: Language in Use","objectives":["Students will be able to talk about abilities and give game rules.","Students will be able to write a sports day poster with abilities, rules and correct punctuation.","I can talk about what my friends can do and give game rules.","I can make a Sports Day poster."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من التحدث عن القدرات وإعطاء قواعد اللعب.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة ملصق ليوم الرياضة يتضمن القدرات والقواعد وترقيمًا صحيحًا.","أستطيع أن أتحدث عمّا يستطيع أصدقائي فعله وأعطي قواعد اللعب.","أستطيع أن أصمّم ملصقًا ليوم الرياضة."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"run","pos":"verb","ipa":"/rʌn/","definition":"to move very fast on your feet","arabic":"يركض","example":"I run around the park with my dad.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"jump","pos":"verb","ipa":"/dʒʌmp/","definition":"to push your body up into the air","arabic":"يقفز","example":"Kangaroos jump on their strong legs.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"swim","pos":"verb","ipa":"/swɪm/","definition":"to move through water with your arms and legs","arabic":"يسبح","example":"Ducks swim on the lake.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"climb","pos":"verb","ipa":"/klaɪm/","definition":"to go up something using your hands and feet","arabic":"يتسلّق","example":"The boys climb the rope in the gym.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"throw","pos":"verb","ipa":"/θroʊ/","definition":"to send something through the air with your hand","arabic":"يرمي","example":"Throw the ball to Majed!","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"catch","pos":"verb","ipa":"/kætʃ/","definition":"to take something that is moving in the air","arabic":"يمسك / يلتقط","example":"The goalkeeper can catch the ball.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"kick","pos":"verb","ipa":"/kɪk/","definition":"to hit something with your foot","arabic":"يركل","example":"He kicks the ball very hard.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"ride","pos":"verb","ipa":"/raɪd/","definition":"to sit on and control a bike or a horse","arabic":"يركب","example":"My cousin rides his bike to the shop.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"team","pos":"noun","ipa":"/tim/","definition":"a group of people who play together","arabic":"فريق","example":"Our team wears green shirts.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"goal","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɡoʊl/","definition":"the net where you score in football; a point","arabic":"مرمى / هدف","example":"Saad scores a goal!","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"whistle","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈwɪsəl/","definition":"a small thing you blow to make a loud sound","arabic":"صافرة","example":"The coach blows his whistle.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"race","pos":"noun","ipa":"/reɪs/","definition":"a game to see who is the fastest","arabic":"سباق","example":"The race starts at nine o'clock.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Today you use all of Unit 6: can/can't, imperatives (do/don't), action words and exclamation marks.\nA poster is short and clear. It invites people, tells them what they can do and gives rules.\n✔ can + base verb: You can run.\n✔ rules with imperatives: Wait… Don't push…\n✔ action words: run, jump, throw, race\n✔ ! for excitement, one at a time","examples":["Everyone can join the race!","Bring your water bottle.","Don't leave litter on the field.","Children can play football and basketball.","Parents can watch from the stands.","Listen to the teachers.","Our team can't wait!","Come and cheer for your class!"],"common_errors":["✗ You can jumps high. → ✓ You can jump high. (base verb after can.)","✗ No push your friends. → ✓ Don't push your friends. (Negative rule = Don't + verb.)","✗ Come to Sports Day!!!!! → ✓ Come to Sports Day! (One exclamation mark.)"],"arabic":"نراجع can وcan't وصيغة الأمر وأفعال الحركة وعلامة التعجب.\nالملصق قصير وواضح: دعوة، وما يمكن فعله، وقواعد.\nتذكّر: Don't + الفعل للنهي، وcan + الفعل الأصلي."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Our Sports Day Poster: Language in Use”. Let’s learn can/can't, imperatives, action words and exclamation marks (unit review) together.","on_screen":"GV-L01-U6-LS5 | Our Sports Day Poster: Language in Use","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Sports Day planning: in teams, choose 3 games. Say who can do each one (\"Saad can run fast\") and give 2 rules for each game (\"Wait for the whistle! Don't push!\").","on_screen":"Language in use","visual":"Split screen: two cast members talking, with speech bubbles appearing."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Today you use all of Unit 6: can/can't, imperatives (do/don't), action words and exclamation marks. A poster is short and clear. It invites people, tells them what they can do and gives rules.","on_screen":"✔ can + base verb: You can run. • ✔ rules with imperatives: Wait… Don't push… • ✔ action words: run, jump, throw, race","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Everyone can join the race! Bring your water bottle. Don't leave litter on the field.","on_screen":"Everyone can join the race! / Bring your water bottle. / Don't leave litter on the field.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “You can jumps high.” That’s not right. We say: “You can jump high.” base verb after can.","on_screen":"✗ You can jumps high.   ✓ You can jump high.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: what is wrong with “No push your friends.”? … Think! … It should be “Don't push your friends.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can talk about what my friends can do and give game rules.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can talk about what my friends can do and give game rules.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: can/can't, imperatives, action words and exclamation marks (unit review).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نراجع can وcan't وصيغة الأمر وأفعال الحركة وعلامة التعجب.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: You can jumps high. — الصحيح: You can jump high.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أتحدث عمّا يستطيع أصدقائي فعله وأعطي قواعد اللعب."]},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"Sports Day Poster – Class 3A","body":"Come to Sports Day on Thursday!\nYou can run, jump, and throw.\nOur team can win the relay race!\nRules: Wait for the whistle. Don't push your friends. Drink lots of water.\nSee you there!","word_count":35,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U6-LS5-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS5-A1","type":"true_false","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read the poster. True or False?","items":[{"q":"Sports Day is on Thursday.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Sports Day Poster – Class 3A”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"You can swim at Sports Day.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Sports Day Poster – Class 3A”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"The class thinks their team can win the relay race.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Sports Day Poster – Class 3A”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"You can push your friends.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Sports Day Poster – Class 3A”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"You must wait for the whistle.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Sports Day Poster – Class 3A”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"The poster says \"Don't drink water.\"","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Sports Day Poster – Class 3A”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS5-B1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Guided practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"Everyone can ___ in the relay race.","options":["running","run","to run","runs"],"answer":"run","explanation":"can/can't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"can ثم الفعل الأصلي."},{"q":"___ talk when the coach is speaking.","options":["Don't","Doesn't","Not","No"],"answer":"Don't","explanation":"Rules: base verb or Don't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"القواعد: فعل أمر أو Don't + فعل."},{"q":"You ___ the ball into the net to score a goal.","options":["swim","ride","kick","climb"],"answer":"kick","explanation":"Choose the right action word.","explanation_ar":"اختر فعل الحركة المناسب."},{"q":"","options":["Hurray!!! Our team won!!!","Hurray! Our team won!","Hurray? Our team won?","Hurray. Our team won."],"answer":"Hurray! Our team won!","explanation":"Use ! for excitement – only one.","explanation_ar":"علامة تعجب واحدة للحماس."},{"q":"","options":["Please wearing your sports shoes.","Please to wear your sports shoes.","Please wears your sports shoes.","Please wear your sports shoes."],"answer":"Please wear your sports shoes.","explanation":"Rules: base verb or Don't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"القواعد: فعل أمر أو Don't + فعل."},{"q":"The children ___ excited about Sports Day.","options":["is","be","am","are"],"answer":"are","explanation":"Use am, is or are to match the subject.","explanation_ar":"استخدم am أو is أو are حسب الفاعل."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS5-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Plan Sports Day. Write your team's ideas.","items":[{"q":"Game 1: ___. Who can do it?","options":[],"answer":"Game 1: sack race. Faisal can jump fast.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses can/can't, imperatives, action words and exclamation marks (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Game 2: ___. Who can do it?","options":[],"answer":"Game 2: football. Ziyad can score goals.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses can/can't, imperatives, action words and exclamation marks (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Game 3: ___. Who can do it?","options":[],"answer":"Game 3: tug of war. Our whole team can pull hard.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses can/can't, imperatives, action words and exclamation marks (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Rule 1: ___.","options":[],"answer":"Wait for the whistle.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses can/can't, imperatives, action words and exclamation marks (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Rule 2 (Don't…): ___.","options":[],"answer":"Don't pull the rope before the start.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses can/can't, imperatives, action words and exclamation marks (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS5-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write your Sports Day poster.","items":[{"q":"Plan: day, games, rules and one exciting sentence.","options":[],"answer":"Thursday; races and football; wait for the whistle, don't push; We can't wait!","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses can/can't, imperatives, action words and exclamation marks (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write your poster in 5–6 sentences.","options":[],"answer":"Come to Sports Day on Thursday! You can race, jump, and play football. Wait for the whistle. Don't push. Bring water. We can't wait!","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses can/can't, imperatives, action words and exclamation marks (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Check: can + verb? Don't? one ! at a time? Fix one mistake.","options":[],"answer":"I changed \"Not push\" to \"Don't push\".","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses can/can't, imperatives, action words and exclamation marks (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Spin the Review Wheel","mechanic":"spin_wheel","rules":["A player spins the wheel and lands on a word.","Say what the word means and use it in a sentence with can/can't, imperatives, action words and exclamation marks (unit review).","Teammates check: meaning (1 point), grammar (1 point), pronunciation (1 point).","Highest total after 6 minutes wins."],"data":[{"cue":"run","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"jump","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"swim","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"climb","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"throw","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"catch","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"kick","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"ride","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"team","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"goal","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"whistle","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"race","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"My grandpa ___ swim very well.","options":["can to","cans","can","is can"],"answer":"can","explanation":"can/can't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"can ثم الفعل الأصلي."},{"q":"","options":["Not run on the wet floor.","Don't runs on the wet floor.","No run on the wet floor.","Don't run on the wet floor."],"answer":"Don't run on the wet floor.","explanation":"Rules: base verb or Don't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"القواعد: فعل أمر أو Don't + فعل."},{"q":"We ___ the rope in the gym.","options":["ride","swim","kick","climb"],"answer":"climb","explanation":"Choose the right action word.","explanation_ar":"اختر فعل الحركة المناسب."},{"q":"","options":["Great job, team?","Great job, team!","Great job, team!!!!","great job, team!"],"answer":"Great job, team!","explanation":"Use ! for excitement – only one.","explanation_ar":"علامة تعجب واحدة للحماس."},{"q":"Can you play tennis? – No, I ___.","options":["don't","can't","cannot to","am not"],"answer":"can't","explanation":"can/can't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"can ثم الفعل الأصلي."},{"q":"___ your name on your bottle.","options":["Writes","Writing","You writes","Write"],"answer":"Write","explanation":"Rules: base verb or Don't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"القواعد: فعل أمر أو Don't + فعل."},{"q":"The coach blows his ___.","options":["whistle","goal","team","race"],"answer":"whistle","explanation":"Choose the right action word.","explanation_ar":"اختر فعل الحركة المناسب."},{"q":"","options":["Penguins cant fly.","Penguins can't fly.","Penguins not can fly.","Penguins can't flies."],"answer":"Penguins can't fly.","explanation":"can/can't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"can ثم الفعل الأصلي."},{"q":"","options":["The players am tired but happy!","The players tired but happy!","The players are tired but happy!","The players is tired but happy!"],"answer":"The players are tired but happy!","explanation":"Use am, is or are to match the subject.","explanation_ar":"استخدم am أو is أو are حسب الفاعل."},{"q":"Choose the best sentence for the poster:","options":["You can play football, run, and jump!","You can to play football!","You can plays football, run, and jump!","You can football play!"],"answer":"You can play football, run, and jump!","explanation":"can/can't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"can ثم الفعل الأصلي."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS5-IMG01","prompt":"A colorful school noticeboard with a Sports Day poster, children's drawings of races and a list of rules, Yusuf and Adam pinning it up. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A colorful school noticeboard with a Sports Day poster, children's drawings of races and a list of rules, Yusuf and Adam pinning it up"},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS5-IMG02","prompt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Fun and Games”, speech bubbles left empty. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Fun and Games”, speech bubbles left empty"},{"id":"GV-L01-U6-LS5-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Spin the Review Wheel”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Spin the Review Wheel"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U6-LS5-T1","script":"Come to Sports Day on Thursday! You can run, jump, and throw. Our team can win the relay race! Rules: Wait for the whistle. Don't push your friends. Drink lots of water. See you there!","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U6-LS5-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Our Sports Day Poster: Language in Use”. Let’s learn can/can't, imperatives, action words and exclamation marks (unit review) together. Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Sports Day planning: in teams, choose 3 games. Say who can do each one (\"Saad can run fast\") and give 2 rules for each game (\"Wait for the whistle! Don't push!\"). Today you use all of Unit 6: can/can't, imperatives (do/don't), action words and exclamation marks. A poster is short and clear. It invites people, tells them what they can do and gives rules. Here are some examples. Everyone can join the race! Bring your water bottle. Don't leave litter on the field. Be careful! Some learners say: “You can jumps high.” That’s not right. We say: “You can jump high.” base verb after can. Quick check: what is wrong with “No push your friends.”? … Think! … It should be “Don't push your friends.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can talk about what my friends can do and give game rules.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"Parrots ___ talk.","options":["cans","can't","can","can to"],"answer":"can","explanation":"can = able to; it is the same for all subjects.","explanation_ar":"can تعني يستطيع ولا تتغير."},{"q":"A cat ___ fly.","options":["cans","can't","not can","can"],"answer":"can't","explanation":"can't = not able to.","explanation_ar":"can't تعني لا يستطيع."},{"q":"Faisal can ___ the guitar.","options":["playing","plays","to play","play"],"answer":"play","explanation":"After can/can't, use the base verb (no -s, no to).","explanation_ar":"بعد can نستخدم الفعل الأصلي."},{"q":"___ you ride a horse? – No, I can't.","options":["Are","Do","Can","Is"],"answer":"Can","explanation":"Questions: Can + subject + verb?","explanation_ar":"السؤال: Can ثم الفاعل ثم الفعل."},{"q":"","options":["My aunt can to bake cakes.","My aunt can bake cakes.","My aunt cans bake cakes.","My aunt can bakes cakes."],"answer":"My aunt can bake cakes.","explanation":"After can/can't, use the base verb (no -s, no to).","explanation_ar":"بعد can نستخدم الفعل الأصلي."},{"q":"___ your teeth before bed.","options":["Brushing","Brushes","To brush","Brush"],"answer":"Brush","explanation":"Imperative = base verb at the start (no subject).","explanation_ar":"الأمر يبدأ بالفعل الأصلي بدون فاعل."},{"q":"___ eat in the computer room.","options":["No","Doesn't","Not","Don't"],"answer":"Don't","explanation":"Negative imperative = Don't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"النهي = Don't + الفعل."},{"q":"","options":["Please to be quiet.","Please be quiet.","Please is quiet.","Please are quiet."],"answer":"Please be quiet.","explanation":"Add please to be polite (no to).","explanation_ar":"أضف please للتأدب."},{"q":"Which one is a rule?","options":["Don't run in the corridor.","The corridor is long.","He can run.","He runs in the corridor."],"answer":"Don't run in the corridor.","explanation":"Negative imperative = Don't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"النهي = Don't + الفعل."},{"q":"","options":["Waiting for the bus here.","Wait for the bus here.","Waits for the bus here.","You waits for the bus here."],"answer":"Wait for the bus here.","explanation":"Imperative = base verb at the start (no subject).","explanation_ar":"الأمر يبدأ بالفعل الأصلي بدون فاعل."},{"q":"We ___ the ball with our hands.","options":["kick","ride","swim","throw"],"answer":"throw","explanation":"Choose the action that matches the body part or thing.","explanation_ar":"اختر الفعل المناسب."},{"q":"The goalkeeper ___ the ball.","options":["swims","catches","climbs","rides"],"answer":"catches","explanation":"Choose the action that matches the body part or thing.","explanation_ar":"اختر الفعل المناسب."},{"q":"I ___ my bike to the park.","options":["ride","play","swim","drive"],"answer":"ride","explanation":"Learn the word partners: ride a bike, kick a ball, score a goal.","explanation_ar":"تعلّم الكلمات المترافقة."},{"q":"Which is the slowest?","options":["sprint","race","run","walk"],"answer":"walk","explanation":"walk (slow) → run (fast) → race (fastest, to win).","explanation_ar":"درجات المعنى من الأبطأ إلى الأسرع."},{"q":"start ↔ ___","options":["kick","catch","finish","win"],"answer":"finish","explanation":"throw ↔ catch; win ↔ lose; start ↔ finish.","explanation_ar":"أزواج الأضداد."},{"q":"Our ___ has new shirts.","options":["goal","whistle","team","race"],"answer":"team","explanation":"Learn the word partners: ride a bike, kick a ball, score a goal.","explanation_ar":"تعلّم الكلمات المترافقة."},{"q":"","options":["Wow! You can jump so high!","Wow? You can jump so high?","Wow!!! You can jump so high!!!","Wow. You can jump so high."],"answer":"Wow! You can jump so high!","explanation":"Strong feeling or urgent command → !","explanation_ar":"المشاعر القوية أو الأمر العاجل ← !"},{"q":"","options":["I can't open the door.","I ca'nt open the door.","I cant open the door.","I cann't open the door."],"answer":"I can't open the door.","explanation":"can't = not able to.","explanation_ar":"can't تعني لا يستطيع."},{"q":"Where do we need \"!\"?","options":["Is this your bag","This is my bag","My bag is red","Watch out, a car"],"answer":"Watch out, a car","explanation":"Strong feeling or urgent command → !","explanation_ar":"المشاعر القوية أو الأمر العاجل ← !"},{"q":"","options":["My brother cannot swim.","My brother can not swim.","My brother can'not swim.","My brother cannt swim."],"answer":"My brother cannot swim.","explanation":"can't = not able to.","explanation_ar":"can't تعني لا يستطيع."},{"q":"","options":["Can you help me!","can you help me?","Can you help me?","Can you help me."],"answer":"Can you help me?","explanation":"Telling sentence → period; question → question mark.","explanation_ar":"الخبرية بنقطة والسؤال بعلامة استفهام."},{"q":"Choose the best rule for a poster:","options":["Don't pushes your friends.","Not push your friends.","Don't push your friends.","No pushing your friend's."],"answer":"Don't push your friends.","explanation":"Negative imperative = Don't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"النهي = Don't + الفعل."},{"q":"How can we fix it? \"he can runs fast.\"","options":["He can run fast.","he can run fast.","He can runs fast.","He cans run fast."],"answer":"He can run fast.","explanation":"After can/can't, use the base verb (no -s, no to).","explanation_ar":"بعد can نستخدم الفعل الأصلي."},{"q":"","options":["Hurray!!! We can go to the park!!!","Hurray! We can go to the park!","Hurray. We can go to the park.","hurray! we can go to the park!"],"answer":"Hurray! We can go to the park!","explanation":"Use only one exclamation mark.","explanation_ar":"علامة تعجب واحدة تكفي."}],"theme_ar":"مرح وألعاب","essential_question_ar":"لماذا من الجيد أن نلعب معًا؟","can_do":"I can say what I can and can't do, give game instructions, and use exclamation marks.","can_do_ar":"أستطيع أن أقول ما أستطيع وما لا أستطيع فعله، وأعطي تعليمات اللعب، وأستخدم علامة التعجب."});
